[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2766602080","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104793#issuecomment-2766602080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104793","id":2766602080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k5v9g","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-31T15:29:40Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T15:30:41Z","body":"We have several other stress tests in the codebase:\r\n\r\n```\r\n8 results - 6 files\r\n\r\ntests/core/math/test_astar.h:\r\n  214  \r\n  215: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][AStar3D] Find paths\") {\r\n  216  \t// Random stress tests with Floyd-Warshall.\r\n\r\ntests/core/math/test_basis.h:\r\n  191  \r\n  192: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][Basis] Euler conversions\") {\r\n  193  \tVector<EulerOrder> euler_order_to_test;\r\n\r\ntests/core/math/test_quaternion.h:\r\n  408  \r\n  409: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][Quaternion] Many vector xforms\") {\r\n  410  \t// Many arbitrary quaternions rotate many arbitrary vectors.\r\n\r\ntests/core/string/test_string.h:\r\n  2146  \r\n  2147: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][String] Empty via ' == String()'\") {\r\n  2148  \tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000; ++i) {\r\n\r\n  2155  \r\n  2156: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][String] Empty via `is_empty()`\") {\r\n  2157  \tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000; ++i) {\r\n\r\ntests/core/templates/test_command_queue.h:\r\n  444  \r\n  445: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][CommandQueue] Stress test command queue\") {\r\n  446  \tconst char *COMMAND_QUEUE_SETTING = \"memory/limits/command_queue/multithreading_queue_size_kb\";\r\n\r\ntests/core/templates/test_list.h:\r\n  542  \r\n  543: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][List] Swap random 100 elements, 500 iterations.\") {\r\n  544  \tList<int> list;\r\n\r\n  549  \r\n  550: TEST_CASE(\"[Stress][List] Swap random 10 elements, 1000 iterations.\") {\r\n  551  \tList<int> list;\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nShould these also be removed?\r\n\r\n> This doesn't look like it's measuring performance per se. \"Stress test\" can also mean it's testing the system under \"extreme load\", acting as a unit test.\r\n\r\nI suppose the closest analogy is fuzzing (to find edge cases that may cause crashes or trip sanitizers), but we don't have a dedicated fuzzing setup (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/168). I agree doctest isn't ideal for this use case, so I'd remove that test as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2766602080/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2766623494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104793#issuecomment-2766623494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104793","id":2766623494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k51MG","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https